<launch>
  <!--
    gazebo_exploration.launch  (v17 — SE(3) drift + IMU bias + outliers)
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Tuning goal: maximum safety in a built indoor environment (hospital, office,
    apartment) while keeping FALCON's planner numerically well-behaved.

    Changes from v16:
      * Drift now composes in SE(3): T_belief = T_drift ∘ T_gt. This couples
        yaw drift into position the way a real EKF does — 5° accumulated
        yaw error after 10 m of forward flight produces ~87 cm of position
        error even with zero direct position drift. Previously the model
        treated yaw and position drift as independent (additive), which
        was unrealistically forgiving.
      * Added slow IMU-style bias state (bias_<ax>_init, bias_<ax>_walk_per_s)
        — the bias rate itself drifts, modelling thermal/calibration drift.
      * Added outlier events (outlier_rate_hz, outlier_pos_std, outlier_yaw_std)
        — rare one-shot pose jumps modelling tracking loss / depth dropouts.
      * Existing per-axis params (jitter_*, drift_*) keep working unchanged
        for small drift the SE(3) and additive models are numerically equal.

    See falcon_adapter.py docstring for the noise model details.

    Changes from v13 (preserved here for reference):
      * SPEEDS lowered for safer turns in tight spaces:
          max_vel     = 0.4   (was 0.5)
          max_acc     = 0.4   (was 0.5)
          max_yaw_vel = 0.6   (was 0.5)   ← higher than max_vel so yaw can
                                            recover at door entries before
                                            the drone is committed
          max_yaw_acc = 0.5   (unchanged)

        At 0.4 m/s a 4m exploration leg produces ~10s splines — comfortably
        inside FALCON's well-tested regime, well clear of the time-allocation
        crash zone we hit at 0.1 m/s.

      * SAFETY knobs corrected to fit standard hospital-door geometry:
          obstacles_inflation = 0.30  (drone_radius 0.25 + 5cm margin)
          safe_distance       = 0.10  (was 0.5)

        The previous 0.5m soft penalty was geometrically impossible to
        satisfy through a 0.9m door — the optimizer was being asked for
        clearance the corridor couldn't provide, so it traded clearance
        for smoothness/goal-cost in unpredictable ways → jamb collisions.

        Geometry rule that must hold:
            safe_distance  ≤  (narrowest_passage_width / 2) − obstacles_inflation
        For a 0.9m door:  0.45 − 0.30 = 0.15 budget → use 0.10 with slack.

      * FRONTIER viewpoint selection rebalanced so FALCON prefers observing
        a new room from OUTSIDE its door (yaw-and-peek) before committing
        to fly through:
          frontier_candidate_rmin = 1.0   (was 2.0)
          frontier_candidate_rmax = 2.5   (was 3.5)
          frontier_min_clearance  = 0.35  (was 0.6)

        With rmin=2.0 the only candidate viewpoint for an unmapped room
        was on the far side of its door, forcing through-door splines into
        partially-known space. rmin=1.0 lets FALCON park just outside the
        door and map through it first.

      * CONTROLLER gains raised for tighter tracking exactly when it
        matters most — entering doorways:
          ctrl_Kp_xy  = 1.5  (was 1.0)
          ctrl_Kp_z   = 2.0  (was 1.5)
          ctrl_Kp_yaw = 2.0  (was 1.5)

      * Mapping scan slowed slightly so depth integration is cleaner before
        the first plan:
          mapping_yaw_rate  = 0.3  (was 0.4)
          mapping_scan_revs = 1.25 (was 1.0)
  -->

  <arg name="map_name"   default="hospital" />
  <arg name="drone_ns"   default="/simple_drone" />

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SPEED KNOBS — tuned for safe indoor exploration
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <arg name="max_vel"     default="0.25" />
  <arg name="max_acc"     default="0.25" />
  <arg name="max_yaw_vel" default="0.6" />
  <arg name="max_yaw_acc" default="0.5" />

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SAFETY KNOBS — sized for ~0.9m doors and ~0.5m drone diameter
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Two complementary mechanisms:

       obstacles_inflation: HARD inflation in the ESDF/voxel map. Walls are
         literally treated as thicker by this many meters. Cannot be
         beaten by the optimizer. Set to (drone_radius + safety_margin).
         sjtu_drone is ~25cm radius, so 0.30m gives 5cm of safety margin.

       safe_distance: SOFT penalty in the B-spline optimizer. Pushes the
         trajectory toward the centerline of corridors. MUST be smaller
         than (narrowest_passage_half_width − obstacles_inflation), or
         the optimizer cannot satisfy it and produces wobbly/jamb-grazing
         splines.

       Recipe by environment:
         Tight hospital/apartment (0.8–1.0m doors):  inflation=0.30 safe=0.10
         Office (1.0–1.2m doors):                     inflation=0.30 safe=0.20
         Wide corridors (>1.5m):                      inflation=0.40 safe=0.40
  -->
  <arg name="obstacles_inflation" default="0.85" />
  <arg name="safe_distance"       default="0.85" />

  <!-- Frontier viewpoint clearance.
       rmin small  → can observe rooms from outside their doors
       rmin large  → forced to plan into rooms before observing them -->
  <arg name="frontier_min_clearance"          default="0.35" />
  <arg name="frontier_min_occ_clearance"      default="0.6" />
  <arg name="frontier_candidate_rmin"         default="1.0" />
  <arg name="frontier_candidate_rmax"         default="2.5" />

  <!-- Controller gains — tightened for accurate tracking through narrow gaps.
       Higher Kp_yaw matters specifically at door entries: if the drone is
       slow to align with the door, the depth camera doesn't see the next
       room and FALCON plans into partially-known space. -->
  <arg name="ctrl_Kp_xy"  default="1.5" />
  <arg name="ctrl_Kp_z"   default="2.0" />
  <arg name="ctrl_Kp_yaw" default="2.0" />

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       TAKEOFF & MAPPING SCAN
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <arg name="auto_takeoff"         default="true" />
  <arg name="takeoff_z_thresh"     default="0.5" />
  <arg name="takeoff_timeout"      default="30.0" />
  <arg name="hover_settle_sec"     default="2.5" />

  <!-- Slower mapping scan + extra quarter-turn means the depth camera has
       more frames per voxel before the first exploration plan, which
       reduces the chance of FALCON committing to a goal in a room it has
       only partially observed. -->
  <arg name="mapping_scan_enabled" default="true" />
  <arg name="mapping_yaw_rate"     default="1.0" />
  <arg name="mapping_scan_revs"    default="1.25" />

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       NOISE INJECTION — per-axis, body-frame model
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Two independent noise sources per body axis (x = forward, y = left,
       z = up, yaw):

       JITTER — i.i.d. Gaussian, fresh sample per callback. No memory.
                Models high-frequency sensor / filter chatter.
                  jitter_<ax>_mean   [m or rad]  constant per-tick offset
                  jitter_<ax>_std    [m or rad]  per-tick std-dev

       DRIFT  — accumulating random walk + linear bias. Models VIO/SLAM.
                After D metres of flight, drift_<ax>(D) ~ N(mean·D, std²·D):
                  drift_<ax>_mean_per_m  [m/m or rad/m]    bias rate
                  drift_<ax>_std_per_m   [m/√m or rad/√m]  random-walk rate

       CONVENIENCE ALIASES — set all three position axes at once:
                  jitter_pos_std        sets jitter_{x,y,z}_std
                  drift_pos_std_per_m   sets drift_{x,y,z}_std_per_m
                Per-axis values take precedence if both are set.

       Reproducible runs: set noise_seed to any non-negative integer to
       fix the noise realisation across runs. -1 (default) = nondeterministic.

       Depth noise (noise_depth_std, noise_depth_proportional) is unrelated
       to localisation and applies independently to the depth image.

       Suggested presets (50 m of flight, isotropic position noise):
         mild      σ≈0.07m  yaw≈2°    drift_pos_std_per_m=0.01  drift_yaw_std_per_m=0.005
         moderate  σ≈0.35m  yaw≈8°    drift_pos_std_per_m=0.05  drift_yaw_std_per_m=0.02
         heavy     σ≈0.70m  yaw≈20°   drift_pos_std_per_m=0.10  drift_yaw_std_per_m=0.05
  -->

  <!-- Convenience aliases for symmetric position noise (default 0 = inactive) -->
  <arg name="jitter_pos_std"        default="0.0" />
  <arg name="drift_pos_std_per_m"   default="0.0" />

  <!-- Per-axis jitter (mean, std) — defaults route to the convenience alias for std -->
  <arg name="jitter_x_mean"   default="0.0" />
  <arg name="jitter_x_std"    default="$(arg jitter_pos_std)" />
  <arg name="jitter_y_mean"   default="0.0" />
  <arg name="jitter_y_std"    default="$(arg jitter_pos_std)" />
  <arg name="jitter_z_mean"   default="0.0" />
  <arg name="jitter_z_std"    default="$(arg jitter_pos_std)" />
  <arg name="jitter_yaw_mean" default="0.0" />
  <arg name="jitter_yaw_std"  default="0.0" />

  <!-- Per-axis drift (bias-per-m, std-per-m) — defaults route to the alias for std -->
  <arg name="drift_x_mean_per_m"   default="0.0" />
  <arg name="drift_x_std_per_m"    default="$(arg drift_pos_std_per_m)" />
  <arg name="drift_y_mean_per_m"   default="0.0" />
  <arg name="drift_y_std_per_m"    default="$(arg drift_pos_std_per_m)" />
  <arg name="drift_z_mean_per_m"   default="0.0" />
  <arg name="drift_z_std_per_m"    default="$(arg drift_pos_std_per_m)" />
  <arg name="drift_yaw_mean_per_m" default="0.0" />
  <arg name="drift_yaw_std_per_m"  default="0.0" />

  <!-- Slow IMU-style bias: an initial value plus its own random walk per second.
       Models how a real IMU's bias slowly evolves (calibration drift, thermal). -->
  <arg name="bias_x_init"          default="0.0" />
  <arg name="bias_x_walk_per_s"    default="0.0" />
  <arg name="bias_y_init"          default="0.0" />
  <arg name="bias_y_walk_per_s"    default="0.0" />
  <arg name="bias_z_init"          default="0.0" />
  <arg name="bias_z_walk_per_s"    default="0.0" />
  <arg name="bias_yaw_init"        default="0.0" />
  <arg name="bias_yaw_walk_per_s"  default="0.0" />

  <!-- Rare outlier events: tracking glitches / depth dropouts.
       outlier_rate_hz = 0.1 means ~one event per 10 s of flight.
       outlier_pos_std/_yaw_std controls the magnitude of the one-shot jump. -->
  <arg name="outlier_rate_hz"      default="0.0" />
  <arg name="outlier_pos_std"      default="0.0" />
  <arg name="outlier_yaw_std"      default="0.0" />

  <arg name="noise_depth_std"          default="0.0" />
  <arg name="noise_depth_proportional" default="0.0" />
  <arg name="noise_seed"               default="-1" />

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       RUN RECORDER — captures voxels, trajectories, coverage curve
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <arg name="run_name"   default="clean" />
  <arg name="output_dir" default="/home/falcon/runs" />

  <!-- BEV publisher -->
  <arg name="bev_xmin"        default="-12.0" />
  <arg name="bev_ymin"        default="-34.0" />
  <arg name="bev_xmax"        default=" 12.0" />
  <arg name="bev_ymax"        default=" 17.0" />
  <arg name="bev_resolution"  default=" 0.15" />
  <arg name="bev_z_min"       default=" 0.30" />
  <arg name="bev_z_max"       default=" 1.80" />
  <arg name="bev_publish_hz"  default=" 2.0"  />
  <arg name="bev_occ_dilate"  default=" 1" />

  <!-- Topic mapping -->
  <arg name="depth_image"        value="/map_ros/depth" />
  <arg name="sensor_pose_topic"  value="/map_ros/pose" />
  <arg name="odometry_topic"     value="/odom_world_gated" />

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Load FALCON config files
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find exploration_manager)/config/robot/uav_model_simulator.yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find exploration_manager)/config/map/$(arg map_name).yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find voxel_mapping)/config/voxel_mapping.yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find pathfinding)/config/astar.yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find fast_planner)/config/fast_planner.yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find exploration_preprocessing)/config/frontier_finder.yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find exploration_preprocessing)/config/hgrid.yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find exploration_utils)/config/perception_utils.yaml"/>
  <rosparam command="load" file="$(find exploration_manager)/config/exploration_manager.yaml"/>

  <!-- Camera intrinsics -->
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/camera_intrinsics/fx" value="320.0" />
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/camera_intrinsics/fy" value="320.0" />
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/camera_intrinsics/cx" value="320.0" />
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/camera_intrinsics/cy" value="240.0" />
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/image_width"  value="640" />
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/image_height" value="480" />
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/min_depth" value="0.1" />
  <param name="/uav_model/sensing_parameters/max_depth" value="5.0" />

  <!-- Transformer config -->
  <param name="/transformer/pose_topic_type"     value="pose" />
  <param name="/transformer/timestamp_tolerance" value="0.05" />

  <!-- Speed limits → FALCON internal time allocation -->
  <param name="/uav_model/dynamics_parameters/max_linear_velocity"     value="$(arg max_vel)" />
  <param name="/uav_model/dynamics_parameters/max_linear_acceleration" value="$(arg max_acc)" />
  <param name="/uav_model/dynamics_parameters/max_yaw_velocity"        value="$(arg max_yaw_vel)" />
  <param name="/uav_model/dynamics_parameters/max_yaw_acceleration"    value="$(arg max_yaw_acc)" />

  <!--
    HARD obstacle inflation in the voxel map.
    Grows every occupied voxel by `obstacles_inflation` meters. The B-spline
    optimizer's distance cost sees inflated obstacles, so the trajectory has
    to detour around them. Cannot be beaten by trade-offs against other costs.
  -->
  <param name="/voxel_mapping/obstacles_inflation" value="$(arg obstacles_inflation)" />

  <!-- SOFT B-spline collision penalty distance.
       Optimizer pushes trajectory toward this many meters from inflated walls. -->
  <param name="/bspline_opt/safe_distance" value="$(arg safe_distance)" />

  <!-- Frontier viewpoint clearances -->
  <param name="/frontier_finder/min_candidate_clearance"            value="$(arg frontier_min_clearance)" />
  <param name="/frontier_finder/min_candidate_occupied_clearance"   value="$(arg frontier_min_occ_clearance)" />
  <param name="/frontier_finder/candidate_rmin"                     value="$(arg frontier_candidate_rmin)" />
  <param name="/frontier_finder/candidate_rmax"                     value="$(arg frontier_candidate_rmax)" />

  <!-- traj_server's startup ramp must stay disabled — cmd_to_vel owns takeoff -->
  <param name="/traj_server/init_dx"  value="0.0" />
  <param name="/traj_server/init_dy"  value="0.0" />
  <param name="/traj_server/init_dz"  value="0.0" />

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Nodes
       ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <!-- Run recorder: saves voxels.npy, coverage.csv, trajectories, summary.json
       The recorder reads /falcon_adapter/* params at shutdown for the noise
       block of summary.json — those params are published below by the
       falcon_adapter node's own private <param> tags. -->
  <node pkg="falcon_adapter" type="run_recorder.py" name="run_recorder" output="screen">
    <param name="run_name"   value="$(arg run_name)" />
    <param name="output_dir" value="$(arg output_dir)" />
  </node>

  <node pkg="exploration_manager" name="exploration_node" type="exploration_node" output="screen"
        respawn="true" respawn_delay="3">
    <remap from="/odom_world"                    to="$(arg odometry_topic)"/>
    <remap from="/voxel_mapping/depth_image"     to="$(arg depth_image)"/>
    <remap from="/transformer/sensor_pose_topic" to="$(arg sensor_pose_topic)"/>
  </node>

  <node pkg="fast_planner" name="traj_server" type="traj_server" output="screen"
        respawn="true" respawn_delay="3" />

  <!-- Sensing bridge: drone → FALCON
       Private params here become /falcon_adapter/<name>, which is what the
       run_recorder reads back at shutdown. Don't add a separate global
       <param name="/falcon_adapter/..."> block — it would be redundant. -->
  <node pkg="falcon_adapter" type="falcon_adapter.py" name="falcon_adapter" output="screen">
    <param name="drone_ns"                 value="$(arg drone_ns)" />
    <param name="world_frame"              value="world" />
    <param name="body_frame"               value="body" />
    <param name="cam_frame"                value="camera" />
    <param name="cam_offset_x"             value="0.2" />
    <param name="cam_offset_y"             value="0.0" />
    <param name="cam_offset_z"             value="0.0" />
    <param name="odom_min_dt"              value="0.04" />
    <param name="depth_min_dt"             value="0.04" />

    <!-- Per-axis jitter (mean, std) — body frame -->
    <param name="jitter_x_mean"   value="$(arg jitter_x_mean)" />
    <param name="jitter_x_std"    value="$(arg jitter_x_std)" />
    <param name="jitter_y_mean"   value="$(arg jitter_y_mean)" />
    <param name="jitter_y_std"    value="$(arg jitter_y_std)" />
    <param name="jitter_z_mean"   value="$(arg jitter_z_mean)" />
    <param name="jitter_z_std"    value="$(arg jitter_z_std)" />
    <param name="jitter_yaw_mean" value="$(arg jitter_yaw_mean)" />
    <param name="jitter_yaw_std"  value="$(arg jitter_yaw_std)" />

    <!-- Per-axis drift (bias-per-m, std-per-m) — body frame, accumulating -->
    <param name="drift_x_mean_per_m"   value="$(arg drift_x_mean_per_m)" />
    <param name="drift_x_std_per_m"    value="$(arg drift_x_std_per_m)" />
    <param name="drift_y_mean_per_m"   value="$(arg drift_y_mean_per_m)" />
    <param name="drift_y_std_per_m"    value="$(arg drift_y_std_per_m)" />
    <param name="drift_z_mean_per_m"   value="$(arg drift_z_mean_per_m)" />
    <param name="drift_z_std_per_m"    value="$(arg drift_z_std_per_m)" />
    <param name="drift_yaw_mean_per_m" value="$(arg drift_yaw_mean_per_m)" />
    <param name="drift_yaw_std_per_m"  value="$(arg drift_yaw_std_per_m)" />

    <!-- Slow IMU-style bias: initial value + per-second random walk -->
    <param name="bias_x_init"          value="$(arg bias_x_init)" />
    <param name="bias_x_walk_per_s"    value="$(arg bias_x_walk_per_s)" />
    <param name="bias_y_init"          value="$(arg bias_y_init)" />
    <param name="bias_y_walk_per_s"    value="$(arg bias_y_walk_per_s)" />
    <param name="bias_z_init"          value="$(arg bias_z_init)" />
    <param name="bias_z_walk_per_s"    value="$(arg bias_z_walk_per_s)" />
    <param name="bias_yaw_init"        value="$(arg bias_yaw_init)" />
    <param name="bias_yaw_walk_per_s"  value="$(arg bias_yaw_walk_per_s)" />

    <!-- Outlier (tracking-loss) events -->
    <param name="outlier_rate_hz"      value="$(arg outlier_rate_hz)" />
    <param name="outlier_pos_std"      value="$(arg outlier_pos_std)" />
    <param name="outlier_yaw_std"      value="$(arg outlier_yaw_std)" />

    <!-- Depth noise (separate from localisation) -->
    <param name="noise_depth_std"          value="$(arg noise_depth_std)" />
    <param name="noise_depth_proportional" value="$(arg noise_depth_proportional)" />
    <param name="noise_seed"               value="$(arg noise_seed)" />
  </node>

  <!-- Closed-loop control bridge: FALCON → drone -->
  <node pkg="falcon_adapter" type="cmd_to_vel.py" name="cmd_to_vel" output="screen">
    <param name="drone_ns"          value="$(arg drone_ns)" />
    <param name="auto_takeoff"      value="$(arg auto_takeoff)" />
    <param name="takeoff_z_thresh"  value="$(arg takeoff_z_thresh)" />
    <param name="takeoff_timeout"   value="$(arg takeoff_timeout)" />
    <param name="takeoff_retry_sec" value="1.0" />
    <param name="hover_settle_sec"  value="$(arg hover_settle_sec)" />

    <!-- Mapping scan -->
    <param name="mapping_scan_enabled" value="$(arg mapping_scan_enabled)" />
    <param name="mapping_yaw_rate"     value="$(arg mapping_yaw_rate)" />
    <param name="mapping_scan_revs"    value="$(arg mapping_scan_revs)" />

    <param name="cmd_timeout_sec"   value="0.5" />
    <param name="pos_cmd_jump_threshold" value="3.0" />

    <param name="Kp_xy"             value="$(arg ctrl_Kp_xy)" />
    <param name="Kp_z"              value="$(arg ctrl_Kp_z)" />
    <param name="Kp_yaw"            value="$(arg ctrl_Kp_yaw)" />

    <param name="vel_xy_sat"        value="$(eval 2.5 * arg('max_vel'))" />
    <param name="vel_z_sat"         value="$(eval 2.5 * arg('max_vel'))" />
    <param name="yaw_rate_sat"      value="$(eval 2.5 * arg('max_yaw_vel'))" />
    <param name="accel_limit"       value="$(eval 3.0 * arg('max_acc'))" />
    <param name="yaw_accel_limit"   value="$(eval 2.5 * arg('max_yaw_acc'))" />

    <param name="ctrl_rate_hz"      value="50.0" />
    <param name="odom_gate_rate_hz" value="30.0" />
  </node>

  <!-- BEV publisher (unchanged) -->
  <node pkg="falcon_adapter" type="bev_publisher.py" name="bev_publisher" output="screen">
    <param name="frame_id"       value="world" />
    <param name="resolution"     value="$(arg bev_resolution)" />
    <param name="bbox_xmin"      value="$(arg bev_xmin)" />
    <param name="bbox_ymin"      value="$(arg bev_ymin)" />
    <param name="bbox_xmax"      value="$(arg bev_xmax)" />
    <param name="bbox_ymax"      value="$(arg bev_ymax)" />
    <param name="z_slab_min"     value="$(arg bev_z_min)" />
    <param name="z_slab_max"     value="$(arg bev_z_max)" />
    <param name="publish_hz"     value="$(arg bev_publish_hz)" />
    <param name="occ_dilate_cells" value="$(arg bev_occ_dilate)" />
    <param name="out_topic"      value="/falcon/bev_2d" />
    <param name="occ_topic"      value="/voxel_mapping/occupancy_grid_occupied" />
    <param name="free_topic"     value="/voxel_mapping/occupancy_grid_free" />
  </node>

  <node pkg="odom_visualization" name="odom_visualization" type="odom_visualization" output="screen">
    <remap from="~odometry" to="/odom_world"/>
  </node>

</launch>